+// RUN (W2-5, ADR 0010): observe.process on processes these tests start, and nothing else. The
+// fixtures (test/fixtures/run) record their own pid and parent pid in scratch (tree/*.json), and
+// that record is the oracle for the tree reax observed through ps; bench/oracle/run.json
+// (scripts/oracle-run.py, no reax code) is the oracle for exit, output, files and shape. Every test
+// runs with REAX_HOME, HOME, USERPROFILE, TMPDIR, TEMP and TMP in a fresh tempBox, so scratch
+// (<tmpdir>/reax-run-*) and the sandbox profile (.reax-sbx-*.sb) land there and can be checked
+// gone. The fixtures' processes are killed only by reax's sandbox code; tests observe them with
+// process.kill(pid, 0). The one process a test kills is one it spawned itself, through its handle.
+// No sleeps: a held run is released by the test (stopOwned, an abort, the deadline), and only
+// process exit and file appearance are polled (20 s at most).
+import assert from "node:assert/strict";
